      "question": "What red‑flag findings would change the urgency to emergent care?",
      "my_answer": "Positive Seidel test (aqueous leak), hypopyon, hyphema, markedly decreased visual acuity (<20/200), severe uncontrolled pain, signs of infection (purulent discharge, stromal infiltrate), intra‑ocular foreign body on imaging, or elevated intra‑ocular pressure.",
